  "name": "resolving-mcp-region-configs",
  "description": "Mandatory Step 0 pre-flight check for regional Google Cloud MCP servers (Composer dak-composer, Dataform dak-dataform, and Dataflow dak-dataflow) before using regional MCP tools or falling back to gcloud/bq CLI. Use whenever a task involves Cloud Composer / Managed Airflow environments, DAGs, or tasks; Dataform repositories, workspaces, compilations, or workflow invocations; or Dataflow jobs, pipelines, or templates, and the expected mcp__*__composer__*, mcp__*__dataform__*, or mcp__*__dataflow__* tools are missing (ToolSearch/deferred tools) or fail on a malformed host. Inspects the live Data Agent Kit plugin MCP config (mcp.json, .claude-plugin/mcp.json, mcp_config.json) across Claude Code, Codex CLI, and Antigravity CLI for unreplaced $GCP_REGION, ${region}, or ${REGION} placeholders, and delegates configuration to @skill:dak-setup instead of editing by hand. Do NOT use when regional MCP endpoints already have a valid region, when regional MCP tools work, or for non-regional services.",
